//
// loft#1430's other half, in its own file because a firing `@EXPECT_ERROR` stops the run.
//
// A REQUIRED visible parameter one implementation does not share is genuinely no dispatcher —
// the dispatcher has nothing to pass for it — and that was already the answer.  What was wrong
// is that it was silent: the abandonment left the call site to fail as a field read, naming a
// field the author never wrote.  It is refused where the implementation is written now, and the
// message names the parameter and both cures.
//
// The `1430` file holds the shapes that must still WORK, which is what keeps this refusal from
// being a way to pass by refusing everything.
//
// @falsified-at: e9f45817 — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/1 -> 1/1 (the
//   suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native the same.  The control emits no diagnostic
//   here at all: it abandons the dispatcher in silence and reports *"field 'sc30' of 'Ra30' has
//   no storage in that type's layout"* at the CALL, which is a different line and a different
//   sentence.

enum Rq30 { Ra30 { a: integer }, Rb30 { b: integer } }

// @EXPECT_ERROR: `sc30` cannot be dispatched on `Rq30`: this implementation takes `k`
fn sc30(self: Ra30, k: integer) -> integer { self.a * k }
fn sc30(self: Rb30) -> integer { self.b }

fn dispatch_it() -> integer { x: Rq30 = Ra30 { a: 2 }; x.sc30(3) }
